From 601530b1f665269cc7ffd54fcad66772b9d785fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CaC033 <34328295+CaC033@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:49:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] claudetui: acknowledge image pastes from the rendered screen

Claude Code can redraw just the changed digit of an image chip. Read the
existing terminal grid from the last input prompt instead of searching
ANSI-stripped output. Keep the current timeout and exit behavior, and
reject earlier prompts and unchanged markers. Document the confirmation
rule and cover split redraws, UTF-8, erasure, and failed-send behavior.

Validated on Windows/amd64, Go 1.26.8, based on 50265256ba. Tests use a
temporary HOME/USERPROFILE and app-data/XDG folders with pinned Go caches
and no real service credentials. gofmt and git diff --check are clean.
The new image tests pass. Restoring only the old pasteImage loop fails
TestPasteImageAcceptsIncrementalRedraw with "did not take an image pasted
as its path: 8", and incorrectly accepts history/no-prompt markers.

Windows go vet ./... and go build pass; Linux go vet -tags nogui ./...
and go build -tags nogui pass. The full claudetui package fails on
TestShimFirstMessageWaitsForTools (0 lines in 30s), matching open #4810.
The package's -race run fails on that same test with no data race reported.
The image tests and TestShimPastesImages pass together with -race.

Full go test -tags nogui -timeout 45m ./... was attempted but the execution
session ended without a complete result; it is not a pass. The real CLI
22-image/mock-API acceptance was not run: no Docker or configured WSL is
available. Keep the PR Draft pending full acceptance; downstream results
are not evidence that this head passed those checks.
